---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ExternalLink from '../components/ExternalLink.astro';
import { event } from '../data/event';
---

<Layout
  title="Enter the competition | TPSP 2026"
  description="The TPSP audition guide for JS1–SS3 students and their parents or guardians. Prepare a portrait video of up to 60 seconds and apply through the existing Google Form."
>
  <section class="guide-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <a href="/" class="back-link">
        ← TPSP 2026
      </a>
      <h1>
        One minute.
        <br />
        Make it yours.
      </h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Your guide to entering the Tranquil Public Speaking Prize.
      </p>
      <div class="guide-summary">
        <span>JS1–SS3 inclusive</span>
        <span>60 seconds maximum</span>
        <span>Parent or guardian submits</span>
      </div>
      <a class="button cream" href="#submit">
        How to submit <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="guide-layout wrap section">
    <aside class="guide-nav" aria-label="On this page">
      <nav>
        <a href="#eligibility">Who can enter</a>
        <a href="#prompt">Your audition prompt</a>
        <a href="#record">Record your video</a>
        <a href="#submit">Submit an application</a>
        <a href="#selection">What happens next</a>
      </nav>
    </aside>
    <div class="guide-content">
      <section id="eligibility">
        <h2>A place for your voice.</h2>
        <p>
          TPSP is open to secondary-school students in{' '}
          <strong>JS1, JS2, JS3, SS1, SS2 and SS3</strong>. A parent or legal
          guardian must submit the application.
        </p>
        <p>
          The audition is online. If selected, contestants attend the physical
          event at the Main Hall, Ilorin Innovation Hub, on{' '}
          <strong>Thursday, 19 November 2026</strong>. The first round,
          semifinal and final all happen that day.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section id="prompt" class="prompt-block">
        <h2>Your audition prompt</h2>
        <blockquote>“{event.prompt}”</blockquote>
        <p>
          Explain the change, why it matters and the difference it could make.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section id="record">
        <h2>
          Keep it natural.
          <br />
          Keep it to a minute.
        </h2>
        <ol class="record-steps">
          <li>
            <h3>Choose your idea</h3>
            <p>
              Think about one change in your school or community. Give yourself
              room to explain why it matters.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Record in portrait</h3>
            <p>
              Hold the phone upright. Your video must be a maximum of{' '}
              <strong>60 seconds</strong>. Include your name, class and school.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Speak in your own voice</h3>
            <p>
              Speak naturally without reading a script. As a recording tip,
              choose a quiet spot and make sure your voice is easy to hear.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Watch it back together</h3>
            <p>
              Check the sound, picture and duration with your parent or guardian
              before submitting.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>
      <section id="submit" class="submission-block">
        <h2>Ready to share your idea?</h2>
        <p>
          A <strong>parent or legal guardian</strong> should open the existing
          application form, complete the requested information and submit the
          audition video.
        </p>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li>Portrait video, no longer than 60 seconds.</li>
          <li>Student’s name, class and school included.</li>
          <li>A response to the exact audition prompt.</li>
          <li>Parent or guardian has reviewed the form and its permissions.</li>
        </ul>
        <ExternalLink href={event.application} class="button purple">
          Open the application form
        </ExternalLink>
        <p class="small">
          Opens Google Forms in a new tab. Google sign-in is required. Submit
          directly there, including any video upload.
        </p>
        <div class="submission-note">
          <h3>Before you submit</h3>
          <p>
            The application deadline, accepted speaking languages, file types
            and upload size limit are awaiting confirmation. Check the form and
            contact the organiser if these details affect your entry.
          </p>
          <p>
            Students in <strong>JS1–SS3 are eligible</strong>. The form’s
            introduction currently says “Senior Secondary School students”; its
            class choices include junior secondary classes.
          </p>
        </div>
        <p>
          Need help? Email <a href={`mailto:${event.email}`}>{event.email}</a>{' '}
          or open the{' '}
          <a href={event.rsvp} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Luma event page<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span>
          </a>{' '}
          and choose “Contact the Host”.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section id="selection">
        <h2>Then comes the stage.</h2>
        <p>
          Auditions are reviewed to select approximately{' '}
          <strong>50 contestants</strong> for the physical event. Fifteen
          advance to the semifinal, five to the final, and the top three receive
          the winner and runner-up places.
        </p>
        <p>
          The organiser will confirm the selection timetable and how guardians
          will receive decisions. Submitting an audition does not confirm a
          place at the physical competition.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/participation/">
          Read about privacy and participation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
  <section class="guide-audience wrap">
    <h2>Coming to cheer them on?</h2>
    <p>
      Audience attendance is free and requires no approval. Reserve your place
      separately through Luma.
    </p>
    <ExternalLink href={event.rsvp} class="button purple">
      RSVP to attend
    </ExternalLink>
  </section>
</Layout>
